Brings `main` up to date with the design-stage work done after #23, so the whole team is on the same pipeline.

## What changed
- **The design stage builds natively in SolidCraft** through SolidCraft's MCP server (always headless, so it never touches a SolidCraft app you have open). `model.sc` is now a native design with named sketches, features and parameters, not an imported solid. `DESIGN_CAD=build123d` (or no SolidCraft installed) keeps the old build123d session.
- **Automatic starting design** (`design/start.py`, no AI). The brief's measured outlines become a SolidCraft design before Claude starts:
  - per-part sketches extruded from height parameters;
  - straight lines, with arcs only at clear corners (no smooth joins, so single faces can be pushed and pulled);
  - named history;
  - parameters on a 0.5 mm grid with comments;
  - one pivot (`pivot_x`, `pivot_y`, `pivot_d`) driving the pin and the pivot hole.
- **Presentation polish** (`design/polish.py`): moulded parts get rounded rims on the top and bottom, as separate features. It is written as `model_presentation.sc` and exported.
- **Design prompt**:
  - reasoning leads and the mesh only advises;
  - the fewest curves and no tangent joins;
  - no pockets, and no components or joints for now;
  - fillets last, rims on both faces;
  - name everything and dimension what you draw.
- **Parts stage robustness** (from the PCB run):
  - no crash on a part with no faces near its seed;
  - "round part" now means a pin-like connector by name, not any cylinder;
  - rejected grows no longer damage labels;
  - no fake joints on rigid objects.
- `model.sc` download in the viewer, a 32 MB SDK message buffer for Claude sessions (photo-heavy tool results), and `DESIGN_NOTES` for per-job instructions.

## Results
- Scissors (design stage only, real capture):
  - kept against the real photos at IoU 0.736 to 0.745, in 104 to 151 s;
  - 13 named parameters and a named history;
  - single-face push/pull works on 76 of 80 side faces (20 of 67 before).
- PCB: the parts stage no longer crashes; the design runs end to end.

## Checks
179 targeted tests pass (design, export, mesh wiring, parts, the Claude backend, config, pipeline, api, intent). The last full suite (1,024) passed before #23. No secrets; no em dashes added.

## Not included (still in progress, on their own branches)
- `presentation/models`: polished demo outputs.
- `docs/solidcraft-design`: the docs update for this work.
- `feat/design`: one unfinished WIP commit.

